# TerraVision — Environment Variable Template
# Copy to ".env" and fill in your own values. ".env" is git-ignored.

# Google Earth Engine
GEE_PROJECT_ID=your-gee-project-id

# --- Optional: lets the Alerts section send e-mail directly ("Send now") ---
# Without these, the Alerts section still offers downloads plus
# "Open in mail app" / "Compose in Gmail" buttons.
# Gmail: use an App Password (Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step Verification -> App passwords).
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=you@example.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password
# SMTP_FROM=TerraVision Alerts <you@example.com>
# SMTP_SECURITY=starttls   # or "ssl" for port 465

# --- Optional: push alerts to field staff on Telegram ---
# 1) Talk to @BotFather -> /newbot -> copy the token.  2) Add the bot to your group.
# 3) Open https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates after sending a message to find the chat id.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC...
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890

# --- Scheduled scans (scheduled_scan.py) ---
# DIGEST_RECIPIENTS=ranger@forestdept.gov.in, team@example.org
# Headless Earth Engine login (service account JSON key pasted as ONE line):
# GEE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type": "service_account", ...}

# --- Storage ---
# Where scans and review decisions are kept. Point this at a persistent disk when hosting
# (Streamlit Cloud wipes local files on restart).
# TERRAVISION_DB=/data/terravision.db

# --- Weather risk (no keys needed) ---
# Forecasts come from Open-Meteo and cyclones from GDACS. Optional: where the "already alerted" record lives.
# TERRAVISION_WEATHER_STATE=/data/weather_state.json
# TERRAVISION_CONTACT=you@example.org     # sent in the User-Agent of place searches (Nominatim policy)

# --- Real-data API keys (see README, "Connecting real data") ---
# NASA FIRMS: free key, real fire hotspots within hours of each satellite pass.
# Get one at https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# FIRMS_MAP_KEY=
# FIRMS_SOURCES=VIIRS_SNPP_NRT,VIIRS_NOAA20_NRT

# Open-Meteo: works without a key for non-commercial use. A paid key (commercial use) switches to
# customer-api.open-meteo.com automatically; set OPENMETEO_BASE_URL only if your plan gives another host.
# OPENMETEO_API_KEY=
# OPENMETEO_BASE_URL=

# Geocoder: free OpenStreetMap search is for light use. For real use, any Nominatim-compatible service,
# for example LocationIQ (check the host in your account): GEOCODER_URL=https://us1.locationiq.com/v1/search
# GEOCODER_URL=
# GEOCODER_API_KEY=
